Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.60,0:00:16.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is going to be quite a chore to find just one book.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.24,0:00:26.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She couldn't be...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.88,0:00:32.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Who's there?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.94,0:00:38.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What do you want, scarred man?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.46,0:00:42.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You look like her. \NBut there's no way you could be...
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.21,0:00:44.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I smell something, I smell something.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.33,0:00:48.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's the smell of an Ishbalan, covered with blood.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.01,0:00:55.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You intend to involve yourself with \Nthe Fullmetal pipsqueak, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.59,0:00:57.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't have that.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.20,0:01:00.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We still need the boy to pursue the Philosopher's Stone.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.85,0:01:02.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:02.95,0:01:05.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Oh dear, perhaps I said too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.96,0:01:09.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Can I eat this one too?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.94,0:01:21.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Man cannot obtain anything \Nwithout first sacrificing something.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:22.66,0:01:26.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,In order to obtain anything, \Nsomething of equal value is required.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:26.95,0:01:31.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That is alchemy's \NLaw of Equivalent Exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.68,0:01:37.99,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,At the time, we believed that \Nto be the true way of the world.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:17.99,0:03:20.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're here! Central!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.47,0:03:24.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Phew! How about we head for the first branch right away?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.04,0:03:26.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother, hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.50,0:03:30.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You don't need to hurry. \NThe library isn't going to run off!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.23,0:03:32.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've finally got a definite lead!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.69,0:03:34.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I can't just sit still now!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.44,0:03:39.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major Armstrong, \Nwe have come to greet you.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.28,0:03:41.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Well done.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.89,0:03:44.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I will be proceeding directly to the command center,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.74,0:03:47.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so you will be in charge of \Nguarding these two from now on.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:48.36,0:03:49.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Maria Ross!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.29,0:03:52.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant Denny Brosh!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.04,0:03:55.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's an honor to meet you, Fullmetal Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.44,0:03:58.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wow, you're dressed just as your second name implies!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.10,0:04:00.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You do indeed wear it with dignity.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:00.43,0:04:02.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This happens all the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.45,0:04:04.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eh, I'm used to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.62,0:04:05.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then it's this little fellow—
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.56,0:04:09.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,N-No, I meant...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.25,0:04:11.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't think you were \Ngoing to be a child like this...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.31,0:04:12.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Aah, enough already!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.67,0:04:15.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Major! We don't need any guards!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.67,0:04:17.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The two of us are both \Nperfectly put back together!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.23,0:04:20.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I really would like to \Nlet you go as well, but...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.01,0:04:24.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We have received information that Scar has appeared again in Central.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.36,0:04:27.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.63,0:04:29.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just put up with it for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.77,0:04:32.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fullmetal Alchemist,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.73,0:04:34.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,please leave everything to us!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.49,0:04:38.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I just hope you don't \Nslow me down.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.75,0:04:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, we have a car waiting!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.27,0:04:44.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I apologize.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.88,0:04:48.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He's always like that. \NPlease don't let it bother you.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.92,0:04:56.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Despite how he appears, he has \Novercome a bitter past many times...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.77,0:04:58.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Please overlook his behavior for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:58.68,0:05:02.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,R-Right... \NBut actually, as it happens...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.65,0:05:08.10,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Last night, the first branch was all but \Ncompletely lost due to a fire that broke out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.83,0:05:11.45,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're kidding me, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.45,0:05:13.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to eyewitness reports,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.51,0:05:16.87,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we suspect that it was the act of Scar, \Nwho is on our wanted list.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.09,0:05:22.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.92,0:05:25.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Our lead is burned to a crisp...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.47,0:05:31.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Really! Seriously, seriously! I want you to hear her too!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:31.34,0:05:34.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's a prodigy! \NAnd she's only three years old!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.95,0:05:37.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She has an angelic singing voice!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.05,0:05:40.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}That settles it! \NShe's going to be a future songstress!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.15,0:05:43.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Colonel, I'm working here.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.01,0:05:46.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? Fancy that! I'm working too!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.36,0:05:48.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Jeez...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.94,0:05:52.49,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I wonder if there is any alchemy that can burn someone up on the other end of the phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.85,0:05:56.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You say such frightening things, \NFlame Alchemist.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.60,0:05:59.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now then, about that other matter...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.64,0:06:03.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,According to eyewitness testimony, \Nwe're certain that Scar was involved.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:04.36,0:06:07.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, looking at the site, I can't \Nbelieve it was the work of him alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.58,0:06:11.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is evidence that he was fighting with someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.06,0:06:12.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Any news on Scar?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.73,0:06:16.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Signs of fighting continue on away from the building site into the sewers.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.39,0:06:21.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We discovered his bloodstained clothes further downstream,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.18,0:06:22.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but we're not sure \Nif he's alive or dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.20,0:06:26.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now in Central, following the death of Brigadier General Grand,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:26.33,0:06:30.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there are plausible rumors going around that Colonel Mustang will be returning.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.66,0:06:34.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Then again, there are others that are putting forward the misdirected notion
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.06,0:06:36.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,that you're the one \Nbehind the disturbances.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.30,0:06:39.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hm, how ridiculous. But then...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.82,0:06:41.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Returning to Central, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.00,0:06:43.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That doesn't sound bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.38,0:06:46.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Watch yourself. You've got a lot of enemies among the higher-ups right now.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.77,0:06:49.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm ready for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.38,0:06:54.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Make as many friends as you can, \Nwho understand you and will support you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.97,0:06:56.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which means,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:56.51,0:06:57.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,as soon as you can...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.33,0:06:59.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,find yourself a wife!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.67,0:07:00.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Shut up!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.49,0:07:02.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Colonel, take it easy on the phone.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.56,0:07:04.48,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lieutenant Colonel! Don't sit up there!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.07,0:07:09.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've been searching \Nsince this morning,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.07,0:07:11.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but these are the only books we were able to recover.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.37,0:07:13.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is terrible.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.78,0:07:15.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.91,0:07:23.25,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Sure enough, there aren't any books \Nauthored by Tim Marcoh in the main building.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.25,0:07:24.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If they had been moved there \Nfrom the branch,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.90,0:07:27.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,there should be \Na record of it, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.14,0:07:30.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, is there any possibility that it was checked out by anyone?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.88,0:07:35.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, but since the circulation records were also burned up...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.73,0:07:37.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.11,0:07:39.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was probably burned up \Ntogether with all the others.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.83,0:07:45.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If only we could have confirmed that his book was really even in there...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:45.04,0:07:47.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Was there anyone else \Nwho worked there?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.21,0:07:51.49,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He and I were the only people on staff in that branch.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.49,0:07:52.97,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just you two?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.97,0:07:56.62,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Only State Alchemists were \Npermitted in the branch, and all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.65,0:08:01.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think I remember there being \Na young lady there who wore glasses.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.71,0:08:04.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, you mean Scieszka?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.63,0:08:06.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She was fired a little while back.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.88,0:08:07.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Fired?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:07.63,0:08:10.17,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That girl was a little unusual.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.17,0:08:12.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka was a bookworm.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.01,0:08:13.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Worm?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:18.51,0:08:20.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess she isn't home.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:20.12,0:08:22.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The lights are on. Let's open it!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.23,0:08:23.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.44,0:08:28.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What a mountain of books!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:28.25,0:08:31.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Does someone actually live here?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.03,0:08:34.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka-san, are you here?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:35.31,0:08:37.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka-san!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.42,0:08:39.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,She's not here.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:40.87,0:08:46.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Help! Help!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.13,0:08:49.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's someone... \NThere's someone buried here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:49.60,0:08:51.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Dig! Dig! Just keep digging!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.39,0:09:02.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.38,0:09:04.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I inadvertently knocked over \Nthat pile of books.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.94,0:09:07.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I couldn't breathe, \Nand I thought I was going to die.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.73,0:09:11.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Scieszka-san, you used to work at the first branch, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.57,0:09:18.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. All I ever did was read books while I was working, so I got fired.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.46,0:09:21.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I have to support my sick mother,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.84,0:09:25.24,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I'm just no good at anything besides reading books.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.24,0:09:29.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, anyhow, Scieszka-san, \Ndo you remember there being a book
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.38,0:09:32.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,authored by someone named Tim Marcoh at the branch?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.48,0:09:33.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tim Marcoh?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.55,0:09:37.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It would probably be a thick, \Nhandwritten research journal.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.72,0:09:42.89,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,A thick, handwritten research journal... \Nby Tim Marcoh...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.94,0:09:47.83,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, I remember!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.83,0:09:51.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was a leather-bound book, \Nwith handwritten manuscripts inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.92,0:09:53.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:53.34,0:09:57.04,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes. I remember all of the books in the branch's collection.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.04,0:09:59.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which would mean, sure enough...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:59.12,0:10:02.33,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Damn. We're right back \Nwhere we started.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:02.77,0:10:04.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.34,0:10:08.10,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, indeed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.10,0:10:11.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It sure is sad when you can't find a book you want to read.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:11.64,0:10:14.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know that feeling terribly well.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.18,0:10:20.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\pos(310,508)}I, too, once wandered among this mountain of books for nearly three days,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:20.05,0:10:24.18,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\pos(310,508)}but I still did not find the \None volume I wanted to read.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.80,0:10:27.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's so, so sad...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.61,0:10:32.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,S-Scieszka-san, thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.02,0:10:34.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With your help, we at least \Nconfirmed that the book existed.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.60,0:10:36.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We'll manage to do \Nsomething from here on.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.59,0:10:39.16,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean, there's still \Nsome other way?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.66,0:10:45.00,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I'm going to transmute the cinders of all the burned books back to their original form!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.00,0:10:48.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Incredible! Can you really do something like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:48.12,0:10:49.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Watch closely!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.65,0:10:55.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh, what about that?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.22,0:10:58.66,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Is it okay for that stuff \Nto go flying off?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.62,0:11:02.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No matter how hard you try, it'll be impossible, Brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.14,0:11:08.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, if you would like, \Nshall I reproduce the book for you?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.81,0:11:14.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I remember the entire contents of a book once I read it.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.02,0:11:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And since I've read most of the books in the branch...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.03,0:11:20.36,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean it? \NCan you really do that?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:20.90,0:11:24.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's a silly little talent I have, but if I can help you out...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.49,0:11:30.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Here you go! \NThere was a lot of content,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.72,0:11:33.21,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,so it took me three whole days \Nto write it all down.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.24,0:11:38.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is Marcoh-san's \Nresearch journal? Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.71,0:11:39.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.84,0:11:44.47,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Everything from light and easy {\i1}hors d'oeuvres{\i0}, \Nto party dinners you'd invite guests to.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:44.47,0:11:47.85,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Tim Marcoh's "1,000 Recipes for Today's Menus"!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.24,0:11:50.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.71,0:11:58.94,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\an8}One tablespoon of sugar, \Na pinch of salt and pepper...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:58.94,0:12:02.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This really is today's menu.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.52,0:12:04.61,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you sure you didn't get the wrong author?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.61,0:12:08.22,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're not serious! All I did was reproduce what I was told to.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.22,0:12:10.54,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It was all in vain, I'm sorry to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.54,0:12:11.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.79,0:12:16.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're sure that, word for word, this is \Nthe same thing that Marcoh-san wrote?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.29,0:12:18.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, no doubt about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.53,0:12:21.07,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're incredible! Thanks!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.07,0:12:21.76,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Ross!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.48,0:12:24.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Give Scieszka this amount of money for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.10,0:12:29.77,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If you go to State Alchemist Services with my references there,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.77,0:12:31.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,they'll take it out of my \Nresearch budget for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.90,0:12:33.27,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.40,0:12:36.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Hold on!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.75,0:12:37.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Sergeant, here.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.19,0:12:44.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,What is he planning to do with a book like that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.01,0:12:45.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Indeed...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.49,0:12:51.00,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Th-That much?!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.00,0:12:53.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,For him to pay out \Nthis amount all at once,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.50,0:12:55.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,he sure is a State Alchemist!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.50,0:12:59.50,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Wait, please! \NWhere are you going?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.71,0:13:02.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We're going to hole up in the Central Library for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.80,0:13:05.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They have abundant materials and dictionaries, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:05.51,0:13:09.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You can't mean it! \NScar's whereabouts are still unknown.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.64,0:13:12.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't guard you in \Nsuch a high-traffic area!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.64,0:13:16.08,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,Well, you can report that to your superiors, \Nor whatever else you like!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.08,0:13:18.06,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is our problem!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.18,0:13:24.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We've finally found ourselves a lead. Sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.58,0:13:33.23,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Marcoh-san's research journal...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.52,0:13:36.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It definitely appears to be \Nan ordinary cookbook at first glance.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.43,0:13:39.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The secret to the Philosopher's Stone \Nis written in here, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:40.22,0:13:43.84,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's encoded, to protect \Nagainst it being misused.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.84,0:13:47.73,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They do say that alchemy was born in the kitchen, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:47.73,0:13:50.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,With me working on this, it'll be a piece of cake!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.78,0:14:30.05,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought I could solve this right away...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:30.40,0:14:32.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is one hard code to break.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:32.68,0:14:35.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If only we could ask \NMarcoh-san directly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.73,0:14:39.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,He abandoned his research.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:39.35,0:14:41.65,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,We can't very well \Nrely on him anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.65,0:14:43.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yo, Ed, Al!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.92,0:14:45.57,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Are you doing all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.57,0:14:48.78,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel! What's the deal? \NWe haven't seen you around at all!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:48.78,0:14:52.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's Scar's appearance. \NHe's got us running all over.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.53,0:14:55.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Al, did you get your body fixed up all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.14,0:14:56.60,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yes, thank goodness.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.60,0:14:59.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those two are on familiar terms with the Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.30,0:15:02.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel Hughes!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.42,0:15:07.24,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,If anything were to happen here, \Nwe could not ensure the safety of these two.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.24,0:15:09.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,They should return to quarters at the Command Center.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.13,0:15:11.14,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I asked you to leave us alone!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.46,0:15:14.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,As long as we do not know \Nwhere Scar is,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:14.12,0:15:16.01,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,we should reexamine \Nour security structure!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.33,0:15:19.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Ross is definitely right.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.58,0:15:21.02,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.38,0:15:23.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,However, I can't make the call \Non my own authority.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.69,0:15:25.52,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why don't you ask Major Armstrong?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.52,0:15:28.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No! Please, not him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:25.52,0:15:28.08,Dialogue Alt,,0,0,0,,No, not him!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.14,0:15:31.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel,
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.88,0:15:34.37,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm just one step away. \NI'm begging you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.56,0:15:39.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm at a point where I can't do \Nvery much about the Scar matter...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.26,0:15:42.69,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,On top of that, all the case records have been burned up.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:42.69,0:15:44.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There isn't any work to be done.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.59,0:15:47.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Case records? \NThose were at the branch as well?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.67,0:15:51.43,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Uh-huh. Affidavit records, \Nlists of names, the whole bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.50,0:15:53.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.14,0:15:57.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Me?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:58.18,0:16:03.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, sure, I've read the military's \Ncriminal records and lists of convicts.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.98,0:16:05.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You'll be fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.70,0:16:09.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,If what you say is true, \Nthis will help us out greatly.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.44,0:16:12.95,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll vouch for her. If you're going to hire her, now's the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.95,0:16:16.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You mean it? To think that I, \Nwhose only ability is reading,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.46,0:16:18.26,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,would become part of \Nthe Court-Martial Office...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:18.26,0:16:20.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:20.03,0:16:23.92,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Working at something really hard is a talent in and of itself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.24,0:16:26.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You have an incredible memory, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.68,0:16:28.42,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I think you should be proud of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.28,0:16:33.51,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:34.00,0:16:38.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Um, I will do the best I can! \NThanks for your consideration!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.35,0:16:42.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,All right! Now that that's settled, let's get right to work.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.03,0:16:44.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I pay handsomely!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.35,0:16:46.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thank you very much!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.20,0:16:52.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I guess I've got no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.93,0:16:57.10,Dialogue,,60,60,0,,I'll send someone from the \NCourt-Martial Office to cover library security.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.10,0:17:00.68,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Eh? Thanks, man. And I didn't even mean for this to happen, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.68,0:17:02.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Liar!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.66,0:17:07.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,See you later. Don't go \Nworking on that too hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.86,0:17:11.63,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Just a moment please, Lt. Colonel!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.77,0:17:15.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Lt. Ross...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.48,0:17:17.80,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I know what you're going to say,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.80,0:17:21.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but they are not the kind of guys \Nwho give up easily.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.42,0:17:25.11,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'll dispatch additional men to you by tomorrow.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.11,0:17:26.56,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I'm asking you to make do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.61,0:17:30.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Why are you supporting them this much?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:30.19,0:17:32.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Letting them continue to work, \Nwhen you know the danger to them...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.67,0:17:34.82,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys are still children!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.82,0:17:37.20,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Which is why we're protecting them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.20,0:17:41.13,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Right now, what they're doing is something that only they can do.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.13,0:17:44.25,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It is the role of us adults to \Nwatch over children like them.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:45.94,0:17:46.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I leave you to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.05,0:17:57.15,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.55,0:19:02.41,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're homunculi, are you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.41,0:19:07.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,My, there are still humans \Nwho believe in our existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:28.18,0:19:29.79,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I didn't get to eat him.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.79,0:19:33.19,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I would've liked to have verified Marcoh's research journal.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.55,0:19:35.81,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,But now there's no need to, is there?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.32,0:19:49.91,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Ah, you're awake?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.45,0:19:53.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a surprise. I didn't think \Nyou were going to come back to life.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:56.64,0:19:57.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Where am I?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.68,0:20:00.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Mister, you're an Ishbalan, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:01.68,0:20:03.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Don't worry!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.46,0:20:05.72,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,This is a town of Ishbalans!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.19,0:20:15.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Grandpa! He's back to life!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.27,0:20:20.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've held on to your life, \Nyoung one.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.33,0:20:24.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're the guy, aren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.39,0:20:26.74,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The one on the wanted list.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.98,0:20:28.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Relax.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.75,0:20:31.71,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There's no one here who would sell out one of their own.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:33.16,0:20:36.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I had no idea there were \Nthis many surviving Ishbalans.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.75,0:20:41.93,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's not just here. There are little villages all over the land,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.93,0:20:44.34,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,and everyone is still going strong.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:44.34,0:20:49.59,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,"The entire world is the \Nbosom of our god, Ishbala."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.78,0:21:04.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,No results today either, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.90,0:21:07.30,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I don't know what it is that they're studying,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.30,0:21:09.67,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,but I wish they would \Nthrow in the towel already.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.67,0:21:13.12,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Those boys won't give up until they've found something.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.21,0:21:17.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And it's our job to protect them.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.33,0:21:20.75,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You've gotta be kidding me!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.85,0:21:26.47,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Now I understand... the reason \Nthis is called the devil's research...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.47,0:21:29.28,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,the reason Marcoh-san \Nabandoned his research...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.28,0:21:30.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Brother...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:30.35,0:21:32.44,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's no wonder!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.44,0:21:34.64,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,The material needed for making a Philosopher's Stone...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.64,0:21:36.35,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,is live human beings!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.39,0:21:40.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Huh? What's the matter?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.83,0:21:44.08,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,And here I thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.08,0:21:47.03,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I finally thought it was \Nwithin our grasp!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.50,0:21:52.98,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You're going?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.98,0:21:54.39,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Thanks for your help.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:54.89,0:21:56.96,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,You {\i1}could{\i0} just stay here.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.96,0:21:58.55,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I cannot do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.18,0:22:02.38,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,I am a person who has \Nbetrayed the way of God.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.59,0:22:10.53,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,That arm is amazing.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.53,0:22:11.58,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:17.41,0:22:20.88,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,It's something very precious \Ngiven to me by my family.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:38.65,0:23:40.46,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,{\i1}Fullmetal Alchemist{\i0}...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.46,0:23:44.29,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Episode 19: "The Truth Behind Truths"
Dialogue: 0,0:23:44.29,0:23:46.31,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,Central 5th Laboratory...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.98,0:23:49.90,Dialogue,,0,0,0,,There is a hell there \Nthat we were unaware of.
